============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-space along which
  the friction factor f is preserved. Physically: a
  simultaneous rescaling of variables that keeps the flow
  invariant (Darcy/Forchheimer regime preserved).

  Generator 1:
    v x exp(+0.999*eps)

  Generator 2:
    dP_L x exp(+0.062*eps), mu x exp(+0.997*eps)
    Meaning: increase mu while increase dP_L
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 3:
    dP_L x exp(+0.809*eps), rho x exp(+0.563*eps), d x exp(-0.059*eps), phi x exp(+0.156*eps)
    Meaning: increase dP_L while increase rho, decrease d, increase phi
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 4:
    dP_L x exp(+0.109*eps), rho x exp(-0.059*eps), d x exp(+0.992*eps)
    Meaning: increase d while increase dP_L, decrease rho
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 5:
    dP_L x exp(-0.289*eps), rho x exp(+0.156*eps), phi x exp(+0.944*eps)
    Meaning: increase phi while decrease dP_L, increase rho
             to keep friction factor f invariant


